  "observations": [
    "The do/while(0) around u2/v2/u3 stores retains loop notes through flow. u1 refs/span change28/29 to29/26, v1 changes16/18 to17/15; global order reverses and UV homes match.",
    "Trace base_2 observes v1 r93 priority45333 taking a1 before u1 r91 priority44615 takes a2.",
    "The independent-product experiment does NOT change the allocating pass to local-alloc. Traces observe global allocations into lo in both variants.",
    "Reused products spanning blocks are evicted from lo and retry into v1/a2. Distinct products have a single REG_BASIC_BLOCK and remain lo after reload; reload inserts mflo t8 for GR consumers.",
    "reload1.c spill_hard_reg has an explicit exemption for a block requiring no spilling in the reserved register class or its superclasses. This is consistent with the observed product survivors; basic_block_needs arrays were not directly traced.",
    "base_4/8 remain98.516%; row=next forces a final stack reload and allocates next before j-offset spill slots; plain row++ causes undesired strength reduction."
  ]
